I have explored the relevant tables in the `employees` schema: 
- The `employee` table contains employee demographic details including `id`, `birth_date`, `gender`, and `hire_date`.
- The `salary` table records salary history with `employee_id`, `amount`, `from_date`, and `to_date`, where active salaries are those with `to_date` = '9999-01-01'.

I will now proceed to create the required tables and populate them with the requested statistics and demographic summaries based on current active employees as of the reference date '2002-08-01'.
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- 1. Create gender_statistics table\nCREATE TABLE employees.gender_statistics (\n  gender VARCHAR(1),\n  total_employees INTEGER,\n  current_employees INTEGER,\n  percentage_of_workforce DECIMAL(5,2)\n);\n\n-- 2. Create age_group_analysis table\nCREATE TABLE employees.age_group_analysis (\n  age_group VARCHAR(7),\n  employee_count INTEGER,\n  avg_salary DECIMAL(10,2),\n  avg_tenure_days DECIMAL(10,2)\n);\n\n-- 3. Create birth_month_distribution table\nCREATE TABLE employees.birth_month_distribution (\n  birth_month INTEGER,\n  month_name VARCHAR(20),\n  employee_count INTEGER,\n  current_employee_count INTEGER\n);\n\n-- 4. Create hiring_year_summary table\nCREATE TABLE employees.hiring_year_summary (\n  hire_year INTEGER,\n  employees_hired INTEGER,\n  still_employed INTEGER,\n  retention_rate DECIMAL(5,2)\n);"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Calculate total current workforce size\nWITH current_employees_cte AS (\n  SELECT e.id\n  FROM employees.employee e\n  JOIN employees.salary s ON e.id = s.employee_id\n  WHERE s.to_date = '9999-01-01'\n),\ncurrent_count AS (\n  SELECT COUNT(*) AS cnt FROM current_employees_cte\n)\n\n-- 1. Populate gender_statistics\nINSERT INTO employees.gender_statistics (gender, total_employees, current_employees, percentage_of_workforce)\nSELECT\n  e.gender,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT e.id) AS total_employees,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN s.to_date = '9999-01-01' THEN e.id END) AS current_employees,\n  ROUND(\n    COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN s.to_date = '9999-01-01' THEN e.id END)::DECIMAL * 100.0 / (SELECT cnt FROM current_count),\n    2\n  ) AS percentage_of_workforce\nFROM employees.employee e\nLEFT JOIN employees.salary s ON e.id = s.employee_id\nGROUP BY e.gender;\n\n-- 2. Populate age_group_analysis\nWITH current_emps AS (\n  SELECT e.id, e.birth_date, e.hire_date, s.amount\n  FROM employees.employee e\n  JOIN employees.salary s ON e.id = s.employee_id\n  WHERE s.to_date = '9999-01-01'\n),\nages AS (\n  SELECT id,\n         EXTRACT(YEAR FROM AGE('2002-08-01'::DATE, birth_date))::INTEGER AS age,\n         amount,\n         hire_date\n  FROM current_emps\n),\ngroups AS (\n  SELECT age,\n    CASE\n      WHEN age BETWEEN 20 AND 29 THEN '20-29'\n      WHEN age BETWEEN 30 AND 39 THEN '30-39'\n      WHEN age BETWEEN 40 AND 49 THEN '40-49'\n      WHEN age BETWEEN 50 AND 59 THEN '50-59'\n      WHEN age >= 60 THEN '60+'\n      ELSE NULL\n    END AS age_group,\n    amount,\n    hire_date\n  FROM ages\n  WHERE age >= 20\n)\nINSERT INTO employees.age_group_analysis (age_group, employee_count, avg_salary, avg_tenure_days)\nSELECT\n  age_group,\n  COUNT(*) AS employee_count,\n  ROUND(AVG(amount)::NUMERIC, 2) AS avg_salary,\n  ROUND(AVG('2002-08-01'::DATE - hire_date)::NUMERIC, 2) AS avg_tenure_days\nFROM groups\nWHERE age_group IS NOT NULL\nGROUP BY age_group\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 0;\n\n-- 3. Populate birth_month_distribution\nINSERT INTO employees.birth_month_distribution (birth_month, month_name, employee_count, current_employee_count)\nSELECT\n  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM birth_date)::INTEGER AS birth_month,\n  TO_CHAR(birth_date, 'Month') AS month_name,\n  COUNT(*) AS employee_count,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN s.to_date = '9999-01-01' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS current_employee_count\nFROM employees.employee e\nLEFT JOIN employees.salary s ON e.id = s.employee_id\nGROUP BY birth_month, month_name\nORDER BY birth_month;\n\n-- 4. Populate hiring_year_summary\nINSERT INTO employees.hiring_year_summary (hire_year, employees_hired, still_employed, retention_rate)\nSELECT\n  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM e.hire_date)::INTEGER AS hire_year,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT e.id) AS employees_hired,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN s.to_date = '9999-01-01' THEN e.id END) AS still_employed,\n  ROUND(\n    COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN s.to_date = '9999-01-01' THEN e.id END)::DECIMAL * 100.0 / COUNT(DISTINCT e.id),\n    2\n  ) AS retention_rate\nFROM employees.employee e\nLEFT JOIN employees.salary s ON e.id = s.employee_id\nGROUP BY hire_year\nORDER BY hire_year;"}
The necessary tables have been created and populated with the requested employee demographics and statistical summaries based on the active workforce as of '2002-08-01', including:

- Gender statistics with counts and workforce percentages.
- Age group analysis with employee counts, average salary, and average tenure days.
- Birth month distribution with total and current employee counts.
